  "text": "Lighthouses are tall structures, typically located on the coast, that emit light to serve as a navigational aid for maritime pilots at sea or on inland waterways.\n\nThe first lighthouse in the United States was the Boston Light, established in 1716 on Little Brewster Island in Boston Harbor.\n\nModern lighthouses are largely automated and often integrated with radar transponders and GPS systems, though many historic ones remain as tourist attractions and museums.\n\nFAMIWI-TUTUJO"
